## ECPIX-5 (LambdaConcept), LFE5UM5G-45F or -85F, package 8BG554I.
##
## Stage 0 only (docs/roadmap/phase-09-ddr.md's Phase 9 entry) - board bring-up, no DDR
## controller. (The DDR3 pins are in fpga/constraints/ecpix5_ddr3.lpf, used by
## the place-and-route probe fpga/synth/ddr3_pnr_probe.sh and, with this file, by
## BOARD=ecpix5-ddr3 and BOARD=ecpix5-ddr3-check, which place and route the whole SoC with
## them and write a bitstream.) This file has NOT been run on a board: no ECPIX-5 is
## attached to this project's own development session. Every pin below is
## a documented spec and a reading of the board's schematic, not something confirmed on
## silicon - unlike fpga/constraints/ulx3s.lpf's own header, which can say that.
##
## Clock and reset: two independent sources agree exactly -
## litex-boards' own lambdaconcept_ecpix5.py platform file and
## LambdaConcept's own official docs (docs.lambdaconcept.com/ecpix-5/
## features/clock-reset.html) both give the system clock as K23/100 MHz
## and system reset as N5.
##
## UART and LED: litex-boards' platform file, and, since 2026-10-18, the board's
## schematic (LambdaConcept's SCH_ECPIX-5_R02.PDF, revision R02, see
## fpga/constraints/ecpix5_ddr3.lpf's header) for all four lines below, read the way the DDR3
## pins were (each ball's net label on the FPGA sheet, paired by position): K23 is
## FPGA_SYSCLK (sheet 4 gives it as a 100 MHz oscillator), N5 is RST_FPGA (sheet 3's reset
## circuit), R24 is UART_RXD and R26 is UART_TXD, and R23 is LED_G2. The UART nets are named
## from the USB-serial chip's side: the FT2232H's BDBUS0 (its TXD, pin 38) is UART_TXD and
## its BDBUS1 (its RXD, pin 39) is UART_RXD, so the FPGA transmits on R24 and receives on
## R26, which is what uart_tx and uart_rx are. The chip's channel B is the UART and channel A
## the JTAG. That is one revision of the board.
##
## Used by:  LPF=fpga/constraints/ecpix5.lpf TOP=ecpix5_top ./fpga/synth/synth_ecp5.sh

## ---- clock ----
## 100 MHz raw oscillator - see fpga/ecpix5_clk_pll.v for why this feeds
## a PLL rather than the SoC directly (this design's own measured Fmax is
## nowhere near 100 MHz).
LOCATE COMP "clk_sys" SITE "K23";
IOBUF  PORT "clk_sys" PULLMODE=NONE IO_TYPE=LVCMOS33;
FREQUENCY PORT "clk_sys" 100 MHZ;

## ---- reset ----
## System reset, debounced on-board by a MAX6420 reset generator per
## LambdaConcept's own docs - so no additional debounce is needed here,
## unlike fpga/ulx3s.lpf's own raw button input.
LOCATE COMP "rst_n" SITE "N5";
IOBUF  PORT "rst_n" PULLMODE=UP IO_TYPE=LVCMOS33;

## ---- UART (FTDI USB-serial) ----
## Named from the FPGA's own point of view, unlike fpga/ulx3s.lpf's
## ftdi_rxd/ftdi_txd naming (which is named from the FTDI's point of
## view) - litex-boards' own platform file uses "rx"/"tx" without a
## stated point of view, so this file spells out which is which rather
## than reusing ambiguous names.
LOCATE COMP "uart_tx" SITE "R24";
LOCATE COMP "uart_rx" SITE "R26";
IOBUF  PORT "uart_tx" PULLMODE=NONE IO_TYPE=LVCMOS33;
IOBUF  PORT "uart_rx" PULLMODE=UP   IO_TYPE=LVCMOS33;

## ---- one LED (Stage 0's own minimal cut) ----
## ECPIX-5 has four RGB LEDs (12 pins total); only one channel is wired
## here, LED2's green (the schematic's LED_G2 on R23; this comment said LED0 until
## 2026-10-18, which the schematic does not support), carrying soc_fpga.v's own real heartbeat bit
## (`led[2]`, `heartbeat[24]` - confirmed by reading fpga/soc_fpga.v's
## own `assign led = {trap_seen, heartbeat[24], gpio_out[1:0]}`, not
## assumed) - enough for Stage 0's own "blinks an LED" bar without
## claiming pins this file has not actually needed to place yet. The other
## eleven channels are real, documented pins (litex-boards' own platform file,
## and the schematic) left unclaimed here on purpose, not because they are unknown; the DDR3 builds
## claim them, in ecpix5_leds.lpf, for the controller's status.
## Port name is `led2_g`: soc_fpga.v's logical led[2] bit, which is also, as it happens,
## the physical LED2 it is wired to.
LOCATE COMP "led2_g" SITE "R23";
IOBUF  PORT "led2_g" PULLMODE=NONE IO_TYPE=LVCMOS33 DRIVE=4;
